# Vendored third-party native trees — clone these, don't commit them:
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/ggerganov/whisper.cpp
#   git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
/app/src/main/cpp/whisper.cpp/
/app/src/main/cpp/espeak-ng/

.kotlin/

# The 3D vehicle model used to be ignored here and installed by
# scripts/select-car-model.sh, on the reasoning that 15 MB of binary does not belong in
# git history. It is committed now, because that reasoning cost more than the megabytes:
# the diagnostics screen needs the diag_v2 model specifically — the one with a motor and
# a battery pack built into it — and every other model in the library renders a car with
# no motor inside. An integrated build shipped with a plain Porsche shell, so the motor
# and battery hotspots had nothing to point at and the cutaway had nothing to open onto.
#
# A required asset that a clone does not get, and that fails by looking almost right, is
# not worth saving space on. The script still works and is still the way to try a
# different model; it is no longer a step someone has to know about.
